{"page":81,"verses":[{"verse_key":"4:20","surah":4,"ayah":20,"ar_uthmani":"وَإِنْ أَرَدتُّمُ ٱسْتِبْدَالَ زَوْجٍ مَّكَانَ زَوْجٍ وَءَاتَيْتُمْ إِحْدَىٰهُنَّ قِنطَارًا فَلَا تَأْخُذُوا۟ مِنْهُ شَيْـًٔا ۚ أَتَأْخُذُونَهُۥ بُهْتَـٰنًا وَإِثْمًا مُّبِينًا","en_translation_id":85,"en":"If you wish to replace one wife with another, do not take any of her bride-gift back, even if you have given her a great amount of gold.","words":[{"pos":1,"ar":"وَإِنْ","en_gloss":"And if","transliteration":"wa-in","verse_key":"4:20"},{"pos":2,"ar":"أَرَدتُّمُ","en_gloss":"you intend","transliteration":"aradttumu","verse_key":"4:20"},{"pos":3,"ar":"ٱسْتِبْدَالَ","en_gloss":"replacing","transliteration":"is'tib'dāla","verse_key":"4:20"},{"pos":4,"ar":"زَوْجٍۢ","en_gloss":"a wife","transliteration":"zawjin","verse_key":"4:20"},{"pos":5,"ar":"مَّكَانَ","en_gloss":"(in) place","transliteration":"makāna","verse_key":"4:20"},{"pos":6,"ar":"زَوْجٍۢ","en_gloss":"(of) a wife","transliteration":"zawjin","verse_key":"4:20"},{"pos":7,"ar":"وَءَاتَيْتُمْ","en_gloss":"and you have given","transliteration":"waātaytum","verse_key":"4:20"},{"pos":8,"ar":"إِحْدَىٰهُنَّ","en_gloss":"one of them","transliteration":"iḥ'dāhunna","verse_key":"4:20"},{"pos":9,"ar":"قِنطَارًۭا","en_gloss":"heap (of gold)","transliteration":"qinṭāran","verse_key":"4:20"},{"pos":10,"ar":"فَلَا","en_gloss":"then (do) not","transliteration":"falā","verse_key":"4:20"},{"pos":11,"ar":"تَأْخُذُوا۟","en_gloss":"take away","transliteration":"takhudhū","verse_key":"4:20"},{"pos":12,"ar":"مِنْهُ","en_gloss":"from it","transliteration":"min'hu","verse_key":"4:20"},{"pos":13,"ar":"شَيْـًٔا ۚ","en_gloss":"anything","transliteration":"shayan","verse_key":"4:20"},{"pos":14,"ar":"أَتَأْخُذُونَهُۥ","en_gloss":"Would you take it","transliteration":"atakhudhūnahu","verse_key":"4:20"},{"pos":15,"ar":"بُهْتَـٰنًۭا","en_gloss":"(by) slander","transliteration":"buh'tānan","verse_key":"4:20"},{"pos":16,"ar":"وَإِثْمًۭا","en_gloss":"and a sin","transliteration":"wa-ith'man","verse_key":"4:20"},{"pos":17,"ar":"مُّبِينًۭا","en_gloss":"open","transliteration":"mubīnan","verse_key":"4:20"},{"pos":18,"ar":"٢٠","en_gloss":"(20)","transliteration":"","verse_key":"4:20"}]},{"verse_key":"4:21","surah":4,"ayah":21,"ar_uthmani":"وَكَيْفَ تَأْخُذُونَهُۥ وَقَدْ أَفْضَىٰ بَعْضُكُمْ إِلَىٰ بَعْضٍ وَأَخَذْنَ مِنكُم مِّيثَـٰقًا غَلِيظًا","en_translation_id":85,"en":"How could you take it when this is unjust and a blatant sin? How could you take it when you have lain with each other and they have taken a solemn pledge from you?","words":[{"pos":1,"ar":"وَكَيْفَ","en_gloss":"And how","transliteration":"wakayfa","verse_key":"4:21"},{"pos":2,"ar":"تَأْخُذُونَهُۥ","en_gloss":"could you take it","transliteration":"takhudhūnahu","verse_key":"4:21"},{"pos":3,"ar":"وَقَدْ","en_gloss":"when surely","transliteration":"waqad","verse_key":"4:21"},{"pos":4,"ar":"أَفْضَىٰ","en_gloss":"has gone ","transliteration":"afḍā","verse_key":"4:21"},{"pos":5,"ar":"بَعْضُكُمْ","en_gloss":"one of you","transliteration":"baʿḍukum","verse_key":"4:21"},{"pos":6,"ar":"إِلَىٰ","en_gloss":"to","transliteration":"ilā","verse_key":"4:21"},{"pos":7,"ar":"بَعْضٍۢ","en_gloss":"another","transliteration":"baʿḍin","verse_key":"4:21"},{"pos":8,"ar":"وَأَخَذْنَ","en_gloss":"and they have taken","transliteration":"wa-akhadhna","verse_key":"4:21"},{"pos":9,"ar":"مِنكُم","en_gloss":"from you","transliteration":"minkum","verse_key":"4:21"},{"pos":10,"ar":"مِّيثَـٰقًا","en_gloss":"covenant","transliteration":"mīthāqan","verse_key":"4:21"},{"pos":11,"ar":"غَلِيظًۭا","en_gloss":"strong","transliteration":"ghalīẓan","verse_key":"4:21"},{"pos":12,"ar":"٢١","en_gloss":"(21)","transliteration":"","verse_key":"4:21"}]},{"verse_key":"4:22","surah":4,"ayah":22,"ar_uthmani":"وَلَا تَنكِحُوا۟ مَا نَكَحَ ءَابَآؤُكُم مِّنَ ٱلنِّسَآءِ إِلَّا مَا قَدْ سَلَفَ ۚ إِنَّهُۥ كَانَ فَـٰحِشَةً وَمَقْتًا وَسَآءَ سَبِيلًا","en_translation_id":85,"en":"Do not marry women that your fathers married- with the exception of what is past- this is indeed a shameful thing to do, loathsome and leading to evil.","words":[{"pos":1,"ar":"وَلَا","en_gloss":"And (do) not","transliteration":"walā","verse_key":"4:22"},{"pos":2,"ar":"تَنكِحُوا۟","en_gloss":"marry","transliteration":"tankiḥū","verse_key":"4:22"},{"pos":3,"ar":"مَا","en_gloss":"whom","transliteration":"mā","verse_key":"4:22"},{"pos":4,"ar":"نَكَحَ","en_gloss":"married","transliteration":"nakaḥa","verse_key":"4:22"},{"pos":5,"ar":"ءَابَآؤُكُم","en_gloss":"your fathers","transliteration":"ābāukum","verse_key":"4:22"},{"pos":6,"ar":"مِّنَ","en_gloss":"of","transliteration":"mina","verse_key":"4:22"},{"pos":7,"ar":"ٱلنِّسَآءِ","en_gloss":"the women","transliteration":"l-nisāi","verse_key":"4:22"},{"pos":8,"ar":"إِلَّا","en_gloss":"except","transliteration":"illā","verse_key":"4:22"},{"pos":9,"ar":"مَا","en_gloss":"what","transliteration":"mā","verse_key":"4:22"},{"pos":10,"ar":"قَدْ","en_gloss":"has","transliteration":"qad","verse_key":"4:22"},{"pos":11,"ar":"سَلَفَ ۚ","en_gloss":"passed before","transliteration":"salafa","verse_key":"4:22"},{"pos":12,"ar":"إِنَّهُۥ","en_gloss":"indeed it","transliteration":"innahu","verse_key":"4:22"},{"pos":13,"ar":"كَانَ","en_gloss":"was","transliteration":"kāna","verse_key":"4:22"},{"pos":14,"ar":"فَـٰحِشَةًۭ","en_gloss":"an immorality","transliteration":"fāḥishatan","verse_key":"4:22"},{"pos":15,"ar":"وَمَقْتًۭا","en_gloss":"and hateful","transliteration":"wamaqtan","verse_key":"4:22"},{"pos":16,"ar":"وَسَآءَ","en_gloss":"and (an) evil","transliteration":"wasāa","verse_key":"4:22"},{"pos":17,"ar":"سَبِيلًا","en_gloss":"way","transliteration":"sabīlan","verse_key":"4:22"},{"pos":18,"ar":"٢٢","en_gloss":"(22)","transliteration":"","verse_key":"4:22"}]},{"verse_key":"4:23","surah":4,"ayah":23,"ar_uthmani":"حُرِّمَتْ عَلَيْكُمْ أُمَّهَـٰتُكُمْ وَبَنَاتُكُمْ وَأَخَوَٰتُكُمْ وَعَمَّـٰتُكُمْ وَخَـٰلَـٰتُكُمْ وَبَنَاتُ ٱلْأَخِ وَبَنَاتُ ٱلْأُخْتِ وَأُمَّهَـٰتُكُمُ ٱلَّـٰتِىٓ أَرْضَعْنَكُمْ وَأَخَوَٰتُكُم مِّنَ ٱلرَّضَـٰعَةِ وَأُمَّهَـٰتُ نِسَآئِكُمْ وَرَبَـٰٓئِبُكُمُ ٱلَّـٰتِى فِى حُجُورِكُم مِّن نِّسَآئِكُمُ ٱلَّـٰتِى دَخَلْتُم بِهِنَّ فَإِن لَّمْ تَكُونُوا۟ دَخَلْتُم بِهِنَّ فَلَا جُنَاحَ عَلَيْكُمْ وَحَلَـٰٓئِلُ أَبْنَآئِكُمُ ٱلَّذِينَ مِنْ أَصْلَـٰبِكُمْ وَأَن تَجْمَعُوا۟ بَيْنَ ٱلْأُخْتَيْنِ إِلَّا مَا قَدْ سَلَفَ ۗ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ كَانَ غَفُورًا رَّحِيمًا","en_translation_id":85,"en":"You are forbidden to take as wives your mothers, daughters, sisters, paternal and maternal aunts, the daughters of brothers and daughters of sisters, your milk-mothers and milk-sisters, your wives’ mothers, the stepdaughters in your care- those born of women with whom you have consummated marriage, if you have not consummated the marriage, then you will not be blamed- wives of your begotten sons, two sisters simultaneously- with the exception of what is past: God is most forgiving and merciful-","words":[{"pos":1,"ar":"حُرِّمَتْ","en_gloss":"Forbidden","transliteration":"ḥurrimat","verse_key":"4:23"},{"pos":2,"ar":"عَلَيْكُمْ","en_gloss":"to you","transliteration":"ʿalaykum","verse_key":"4:23"},{"pos":3,"ar":"أُمَّهَـٰتُكُمْ","en_gloss":"(are) your mothers","transliteration":"ummahātukum","verse_key":"4:23"},{"pos":4,"ar":"وَبَنَاتُكُمْ","en_gloss":"and your daughters","transliteration":"wabanātukum","verse_key":"4:23"},{"pos":5,"ar":"وَأَخَوَٰتُكُمْ","en_gloss":"and your sisters","transliteration":"wa-akhawātukum","verse_key":"4:23"},{"pos":6,"ar":"وَعَمَّـٰتُكُمْ","en_gloss":"and your father's sisters","transliteration":"waʿammātukum","verse_key":"4:23"},{"pos":7,"ar":"وَخَـٰلَـٰتُكُمْ","en_gloss":"and your mother's sisters","transliteration":"wakhālātukum","verse_key":"4:23"},{"pos":8,"ar":"وَبَنَاتُ","en_gloss":"and daughters","transliteration":"wabanātu","verse_key":"4:23"},{"pos":9,"ar":"ٱلْأَخِ","en_gloss":"(of) brothers","transliteration":"l-akhi","verse_key":"4:23"},{"pos":10,"ar":"وَبَنَاتُ","en_gloss":"and daughters","transliteration":"wabanātu","